From 11d4139f2ae08e43c6b63a8bb675d8bd701cadea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:10:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 124/143] drm/sun4i: sun55i_de: only the primary plane accepts
 AFBC modifiers

The v35x overlay (LAY1..3) and cursor planes are registered with a
LINEAR-only modifier list, but the plane's .format_mod_supported
callback (shared with the primary) returns true for the supported AFBC
modifier on every plane of an RCQ mixer.  drm_plane_has_format()
consults the callback INSTEAD of the per-plane modifier list when it is
set, so the atomic plane check accepted an AFBC framebuffer on the
overlay/cursor planes even though only the primary's channel has the
AFBD decoder wired: the staging code (sun55i_de_ovl_stage /
sun55i_de_cursor_stage) then dropped the layer silently and the commit
scanned out nothing where the plane should be.

This also broke the atomic-reject contract the overlay planes rely on:
an invalid configuration must fail atomic_check so the compositor falls
back to GPU composition, never succeed and display wrong.

Gate the AFBC path on the exact plane that feeds the AFBD (UI logical
channel 1, layer 0).  The advertised IN_FORMATS blobs do not change
(they are built from the per-plane modifier lists, which were already
LINEAR-only for the overlay/cursor planes).

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c
index fcff35e39..9af04eecf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c
@@ -456,6 +456,15 @@ static bool sun8i_ui_layer_format_mod_supported(struct drm_plane *plane,
 		return true;
 	if (!layer->mixer || !layer->mixer->cfg->uses_rcq)
 		return false;
+	/*
+	 * Only the primary (channel 1 layer 0) feeds the AFBD; the LAY1..3
+	 * overlays and the cursor channel scan out LINEAR only.  This callback
+	 * overrides the per-plane modifier list in drm_plane_has_format(), so
+	 * without this check an AFBC fb on an overlay/cursor plane would pass
+	 * atomic_check and then be silently dropped by the staging code.
+	 */
+	if (layer->overlay != 0 || layer->channel != SUN55I_DE_OVL_UI_LOGIC_CHN)
+		return false;
 	return sun55i_de_afbc_mod_supported(format, modifier);
 }
 
